From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: name the display's LUTDMA registers

The DPU's LUTDMA engine sits at 0x0aeac000, between the MDP and VBIF
regions. The driver maps it as "regdma" when present, and loads the
DSPP's IGC table through it.

Signed-off-by: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
@@ -4089,8 +4089,9 @@
 			mdss_mdp: display-controller@ae01000 {
 				compatible = "qcom,sm8550-dpu";
 				reg = <0 0x0ae01000 0 0x8f000>,
-				      <0 0x0aeb0000 0 0x3000>;
-				reg-names = "mdp", "vbif";
+				      <0 0x0aeb0000 0 0x3000>,
+				      <0 0x0aeac000 0 0x800>;
+				reg-names = "mdp", "vbif", "regdma";
 
 				interrupt-parent = <&mdss>;
 				interrupts = <0>;
